  "notes": "The Harmony 800 (USB 046d:c127, MH protocol): a touchscreen remote with a slide-out keyboard. Configurations are generated from the project with the Harmony One's generator on the 800's GSGD format (backends/harmony_800) and written as the zip Concordance sends to /cfg/usercfg; writing needs a libconcord that knows the 800 (concordance-fork, branch harmony-800). Afterglow reads back only configurations it built. The front panel's key codes and the seven LEDs were read off asdfgpio's 800 with the key and light tests; Mouse is kept for the touchpad, and the keyboard is still to be bound. Learning is off.",
  "schema": "afterglow-remote/1",
  "vocabulary": {
